    <string name="tbb_help_title">How to play Toy Baseball</string>
    <string name="tbb_help_text">Score more runs than your rival over 3, 5 or 9 innings. Each pitch is a duel, and you swap between pitching and batting every half-inning.\n\nPITCHER: choose a pitch and a spot on the 5x5 grid, then Throw. The middle 3x3 is the strike zone. Fastball is the fastest, then slider, curveball and changeup.\n\nBATTER: without seeing the pitch, choose which pitch you are ready for (your timing) and a spot in the strike zone to aim at, then Swing, or Take if you think it will be a ball. A Contact swing is forgiving; a Power swing needs a better guess but can clear the fence.\n\nThen the pitch is revealed. A good guess of both speed and place means a hard hit; a poor one means a miss, a foul or an easy out. Four balls are a walk, three strikes are an out, three outs end the half-inning. The history of pitches shows what your rival likes to do.\n\nIn Pass and Play, each side\'s choice is hidden behind a hand-over card.</string>
